        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Alternatively, the Lamb–Oseen [10, 18] or Newman [17] vortex can be fitted to the data. These are also written in terms of  $ V_{s,max} $ and  $ r_c $, but the radial distribution function is different and a factor  $ \\alpha $ of an exponential function defines the shape. Expanding the parameter  $ \\alpha $ to the inclusion of the vortex age  $ \\psi_v $ the Hamel–Oseen [5] model can be used as well.",
          "block_bbox": [
            600,
            908,
            1098,
            1070
          ],
          "block_id": 14,
          "block_order": 9,
          "group_id": 14,
